{"parseRefreshTokenResponse injects literal string 'refresh_token' as refresh_token when response lacks one - this placeholder value gets stored and later causes opaque auth errors when used for refresh grants": 0.946911633014679, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses z.string().toString() as literal key - evaluates to Zod internal string representation instead of wildcard key matcher, causing token validation to be bypassed or incorrectly reject valid responses": 0.9105919599533081, "Google Calendar stores SafeParseResult wrapper instead of credential data - parseRefreshTokenResponse returns the full Zod SafeParseReturnType object instead of the parsed data, causing the wrong shape to be written to the database": 0.9733268618583679, "refreshOAuthTokens returns fetch Response instead of expected types when APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED is true - callers expect parsed data but receive raw Response object, breaking Google Calendar and HubSpot token refresh": 0.509316086769104, "Salesforce response.statusText check fails under HTTP/2 - statusText is empty string under HTTP/2 regardless of status code, causing successful 200 responses to be treated as errors": 0.7119341492652893, "Webhook endpoint does not validate HTTP method - app-credential handler processes any HTTP method without checking req.method, allowing GET requests to trigger credential creation/update": 0.9877164959907532, "Salesforce creates jsforce connection with stale pre-refresh tokens - after refreshing tokens, the Connection is created using original credentialKey values instead of the new accessTokenParsed.data values": 0.9350430965423584}